        <mxCell id="8dAbgZd29Mcq3z_WeXtU-62" value="This is done using two simple 2-DOF(kinda 2x 3d printers but as grippers) robots, which take the brackets, move them horizontally, and grip onto the pulley. This ensures that the bracket and pulley are positioned correctly relative to each other." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="30" y="530" width="260" height="90" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="8dAbgZd29Mcq3z_WeXtU-63" value="The robots then move the two brackets and pulley vertically down, placing them onto the base. A screwing module can then be used to fasten the two brackets and pulley onto the base." style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" vertex="1" parent="1">
